  "interpretation": [
    "2x the one-payload copy rate represents combined read/write traffic; 1x is the slower sensitivity. Each traffic arm assumes full exposure at that rate with stage-duration caps. Only the dedicated free_merge_and_gap arm erases the whole merge and its following gap with free added compute/second input access in HcPost. It retains HcPost apart from one read and holds other work fixed. No F21, routing, expert or weight placement credit.",
    "Every BF16 shared Down and routed result must match stock. Round their sum to BF16 before HcPost, keep its ordered four products and BF16 output for later readers. Down epilogue is conditional on local tile transfer with both rounded inputs available, original post scale/combination order, and no additional Down observer. Independent readers may require materialization or a second output.",
    "Premix-only carries forward exactly one 4x5120 BF16 residual read at the 34 direct following attention entries. Keep residual/global writes and coefficients, the second residual read and Y/norm. Keep both Engram updates, three auxiliary entries and final terminal work. Joint and marginal arms share a clock correction per layer and original branch/shape. No sum with the earlier paired-boundary budget.",
    "Fixed four eager waves, 39 next DispatchFFNCombine starts and one last HcPost completion per rank and wave. Propagate surviving latest-rank advance in series through the own first eager wave (or all four for makespan), with all other intervals translating. A different inter-wave or downstream dependency can mask gains. Clock bounds are sensitivities, not confidence intervals.",
    "Keep q=3 on stock for both graph and eager. Ordinary six requests use their archived eager rank-row counts, 40 merges and 34 direct premix entries, the median calibrated rate and no task cap at their unprofiled shapes. All savings reach that response. No traffic weights or population estimate.",
    "Archived kernel shape proxy linearly interpolates signed native-minus-fused median differences at M3,211,1023; not a fitted performance law or an actual timing at the frozen eager shapes. No new service or hardware measurements."
  ],
